.TH IMPROVE 1 "September 2026" "improve 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
improve \- measure one proposed source change on fresh cases
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B improve
.RB [ \-n ]
.RB [ \-o " NEW_DIRECTORY" ]
< experiment.json
.br
.B improve verify
.RB [ \-record " EXECUTABLE" ]
DIRECTORY
.br
.B improve version
.SH DESCRIPTION
Reads one version-1 JSON specification and orchestrates caller-selected
proposer, trial/scorer and judge commands with literal argv and JSON pipes.
Snapshots source and cases, pins commands and declared dependencies, measures
development baselines, proposes one change, compares fresh development pairs,
and tests the frozen candidate on reserved cases only after development passes.
Alternates pair order across repeats. Uses Record to capture and replay each
process boundary. No provider client, agent loop, retry, resume or scheduler.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-n
Validate inputs and print maximum workload. Execute no commands and create no files.
.TP
.BI \-o " DIRECTORY"
Select a new output directory with an existing parent, disjoint from all inputs.
.TP
.BI "verify \-record " EXECUTABLE
Select Record for offline verification; default is record on PATH.
.SH SPECIFICATION
Required fields: version (1), source, mutable, development, holdout, commands.
Each case has id, family and file. IDs are unique; families and identical file
bytes may not overlap across splits. Commands has propose, trial and judge,
each with an argv array. Optional dependencies lists files to pin. Settings is
opaque JSON passed to commands. Record selects its executable, default record.
Defaults: repeats 3, command_seconds 180, max_seconds 2400.
Allowed: 2-10 repeats, 1-20 cases per split, 1-64 mutable existing UTF-8 files.
Only existing selected files can be replaced; modes are preserved.
.PP
JSON and captured streams are bounded at 2 MiB. Stream overflow cancels the
command group and retains an incomplete bounded prefix. Source and command
trees permit 4096 regular files and 128 MiB; the whole study permits 8192 files
and 512 MiB. The per-file limit is 64 MiB. Planning rejects unavoidable source
copies exceeding the study bound and call ledgers above 1 MiB; command-written files are not disk-quota
controlled. Admitted runs emit invalid-evidence JSON on finalization failure
and remove any proposal export. Data paths refuse symlinks; executable links
are resolved once. Paths are relative to the invoking directory; argv arguments
remain literal and scripts should use absolute paths. Declare transitive
files explicitly. Hashes do not freeze environment or remote services.
.SH COMMAND CONTRACT
The proposer receives source, mutable files, development cases and observations,
settings, work and evidence paths. Exit 0 returns version, hypothesis, changes
(path/content replacements) and cost. Exit 1 supplies no proposal.
.PP
Trials receive a fresh source copy, case descriptor, repeat, settings, work and
evidence. Exit 0 returns version, non-null score and cost. Job failure belongs
in the score; a failed adapter is an incomplete measurement.
.PP
The judge receives paired baseline/candidate samples, split and settings.
Return version, decision (keep or discard), reason and cost. Keep requires
exit 0; discard requires exit 1. Other outcomes are errors.
.PP
Cost is nonnegative provider dollars or null. Unknown cost remains unknown in
the total; known_cost is only a subtotal. Include nested/repair/authoring costs.
See README.md for exact JSON requests and examples.
.SH OUTPUT
One JSON result on stdout; diagnostics on stderr. The evidence directory retains
requests, streams, Record receipts, scores, decisions, snapshots and inventory.
Supported results export proposal/source and a manifest binding source hashes.
The original source is never updated and no release is published.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0: supported proposal or successful planning/verification.
.br
1: no supported proposal or incomplete execution.
.br
2: invalid invocation, broken evidence or operational error.
.SH VERIFICATION
Verify checks retained hashes and Record replay without running the original
commands. It refuses incomplete receipts. It does not rerun a judge, validate
current external dependencies, prove label correctness or authorize deployment.
Missing final inventory means incomplete evidence.
.SH BOUNDARIES
Selected commands are trusted programs and choose their own confinement through
existing tools. Holdout separation is procedural, not filesystem secrecy.
Timeouts signal the process group and permit three seconds of cleanup before
escalation; detached descendants remain the runner's responsibility.
Weigh is optional inside caller-selected research commands, never implicit.
Hone's checked-recovery contract is independent of experiment comparisons.
.SH SEE ALSO
record(1), agent(1), hire(1), ask(1), hone(1), cage(1)
